        description
            Build Compiled and the compiler: @spec.Compile and @spec.Diagnostics from the public API.

            **Why now:** the skeleton compiles only the Pay machine; the full construction rules and the
            diagnostics are unbuilt, and every module after this reads Compiled.

            **Read first:** @spec.Compile, @spec.Diagnostics, @task.V3.T13 (the static cases that judge it),
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the round-14 carry list).

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): name the author-facing
            features, each passing a case on production: Flow.input, computed Flow.initial, Flow.private, one source per
            field, ImpureDefault, creation purity, identity and fragment inputs, compound states and Flow.state traits,
            context slots, the Definition Schemas, E.X with InvalidEvent, payload checks and app entries (rows M03 to
            M16, M19 to M21, M35 to M37, M39 to M41, R01 to R03; @plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1). Also own
            handler(), guard(), Flow.state and the "Flow outermost" type rule (M05, M13, M22), which no Spec states, and
            Invariants for Compile R10, R13 and R14 (a Spec revision). **Owed checks** (no Invariant or case today):
            M06, M19, M39, M40, M41 (Compile R14), M23, M24, M27, M28 (Compile R10) and M33 (Compile R11).

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1, @plan.Diagnostics.O1.

            **Slice 3, machine structure (replan, accepted 2026-11-11):** the compiler and turn for compound states,
            history, traits and fragments, `.each`, raise and notify, `Flow.input` (compile half; the naming half is
            slice 4), computed initial, private fields and `check()`; Diagnostics with multi-violation errors; schedules
            (multi-step, `restartOn`, keyed, `disarmOn`, metadata). Absorbs the Turn rows of @task.V3.T8 (I1, I4, I6,
            I24, I35, I16, I18, I32 to I34, each with its evidence; T8 is closed as moved), the turn features
            @task.V3.T18 held (M42 to M63, M68, M69, M71 to M73), the fragments of @task.V3.T21 and the owed check M66 
            (Turn
            R18, freeze releases placements; it left with T8's scope and T21's fragments). Codes: cs hs fr ea
            rn ci pv ck ms rs ks dm, and the catalogue 5B codes su nf rz ro po. Parts built: S20 [C]; S06 [H]; S15 [G];
            S07 [I]; S14 [D]; and, with the subset available, S28 [J] and S29 [K], which gain operations in slices 4, 5,
            7 and 9 as their codes land. Turn R4 (history) and R23 (snapshot) each get an Invariant. Bench: turn cost on
            compound parts (S06, S20); memory per `.each` copy (S15). Effort 8 (estimate); split at schedules if
            first-contact reds pile up. Read first: code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md
            (part 3, "3 Machine structure") and
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/fixture-catalogue-2026-11-11.md (5B, "Composites and the
            matrix").

            **Phase-out, step 5 (the user accepted 2026-11-11):** the Release (trait, `whenAbandoned`) and Form twins
            are written in `fixtures/`, and the model's Turn section replaces the Turn helper tables (`turn/selection`,
            `anchor`, `phases`, `late`) once it catches every mutant they caught (V1); run the hand cases on each
            fixture on production; write production mutants per oracle the slice judges, mapped by Invariant from the
            round-14 mutants; delete the descriptor once the derived reference equals it (rest of `one-lane.ts` and
            `form.ts` go). Read code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md.

            **Moved to @task.V3.T47:** the production static surface (`construct`, data view); this Task builds the
            rest of it (CLI part and diagnostics).

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** pins matching output rather than the Spec → caught by T13's cited
              cases.
            - **Gates:** static cases; `nub run check`.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            - The Compile and Diagnostics cases pass on production.
            - Flow.input, computed Flow.initial, Flow.private, the Definition Schemas, E.X with InvalidEvent, payload
              checks, compounds, Flow.state traits, context slots and app entries each pass a case on production
              (@plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1).
            - Compile R10, R13 and R14 each have an Invariant, and handler(), guard(), Flow.state and the "Flow
              outermost" rule a case; the owed checks above exist.
            - The Turn rows moved from @task.V3.T8 (I1, I4, I6, I24, I35, I16, I18, I32 to I34) pass on production, each
              with its evidence.
            - Compounds, history, raise and notify, disarmOn, schedule keys and metadata, and the snapshot shape pass
              cases on production (@plan.Machines.O2 to O8).
            - Fragments (traits, subroutines, `.each`, nested) pass cases on production.
            - M66 has a check: freeze releases placements (Turn R18).
            - The slice's generated runs pass on production, and its benchmark replay matches the work fingerprint.
            - Declared: cs hs fr ea rn ci pv ck ms rs ks dm su nf rz ro po are in the production and Spec-model
              capability lists, and the feature-matrix gate shows none of them as owed.
            - Enabled: S20, S06, S15, S07, S14, and J and K with their available subsets declare those codes among their
              needs, the generator draws their operations, and the app mix runs them.
            - Covered: the combination gate counts the pairs among implemented codes, fails an unexercised interacting
              pair with no dated waiver, and passes before this Task closes.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
            - Phase-out step 5: the Release and Form twins exist in `fixtures/`; the model's Turn section catches every
              mutant the Turn helper tables caught, and those tables are deleted; the same verdict per case on round-14
              and production.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist;
              Compile static cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
