        description
            Build operations with the required services list and @spec.Reads, with the round-14 carry list's
            unbuilt design items (slice 5).

            **Why now:** the runtime cannot yet declare fragments or operations, or read resources, which
            the Reads area and the carry items judge.

            **Read first:** @spec.Reads, @spec.Compile.R9, @spec.Compile.R10, @spec.Compile.R11,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the round-14 carry list: the "design items not
            built" row).

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): name the Reads features
            that spec-split.md sets for "when the operations module reaches them", and write their Spec section first:
            staleTime and gcTime, trailing refetch, focus and connection triggers, holds, invalidate and clear, setData,
            write batches (256), optimistic stacking, placeholders and contract.get, key bounds and InvalidKey (rows
            P12, P15, P16, P20, P21, P23, P28, P44, P45, P47, P50; @plan.Operations.O1, O2, O5, O6). Add an Invariant
            for Reads R8 (P22, P24, both owed checks). The user may split this into its own Task; if so, record it in a
            note.

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Operations.O1, @plan.Operations.O2, @plan.Operations.O5, @plan.Operations.O6.

            **Slice 5, reads (replan, accepted 2026-11-11):** absorbs @task.V3.T12 (the Reads oracles `lookups` and
            `optimistic`; the mutants `drain.*` and `lie.settled-*`). Fragments moved to @task.V3.T17. The world gains
            focus, online and an offline span. Adds the Reads oracles, lookups shared by key, `subscribe` and the lifted
            Reads Q2 section (freshness, refetch, holds, cache writes, batches, placeholders, key bounds, triggers,
            stacking). Codes: sb fz sw ph kb os op of. Parts built: S02, S26, S18 and S11 without streams [F]; J gains
            its lookup operations. It completes F and G and adds the most pairs of any slice. Bench: retained entries
            (S26); burst linearity, 10,000 against 100,000 events, ratio under 30 (S02). Effort 7 (estimate). Read
            first: code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md (part 3, "5 Reads").

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a carry item marked built with no case → caught by the completion
              audit.
            - **Gates:** the suite; falsify.
            - **Stops:** a large public API change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            - The Reads area and every carry item's case pass on production.
            - The Reads features above pass cases on production, and Reads has a Spec section for them.
            - Reads R8 has an Invariant (subscribe starts a request only when missing; no automatic retry).
            - Every Reads Invariant has its oracle or case and each oracle kills its mutants (from @task.V3.T12).
            - The slice's generated runs pass on production, and its benchmark replay matches the work fingerprint.
            - Declared: sb fz sw ph kb os op of are in the production and Spec-model capability lists, and the
              feature-matrix gate shows none of them as owed.
            - Enabled: S02, S26, S18, S11, and J's lookup operations declare those codes among their needs, the
              generator draws their operations, and the app mix runs them.
            - Covered: the combination gate counts the pairs among implemented codes, fails an unexercised interacting
              pair with no dated waiver, and passes before this Task closes.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
